        "content": "<p>subotac opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14063\">PR #14063</a> from <code>subotac:fix/dse-divergent-store</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Fixes #14053.</p>\n<p>Cranelift's post-dominator tree only considers paths that reach an explicit CFG exit. Dead-store elimination could therefore treat an overwriting store as inevitable even when another path entered a divergent region,<br>\n  where a trap could expose the earlier memory state.</p>\n<p>Reject cross-block dead-store candidates when the original store can reach a divergent block without first passing through the overwriter. Add a CLIF regression covering the divergent path.</p>\n<p>Testing:</p>\n<p>- all 38 alias-analysis filetests<br>\n  - all 187 <code>cranelift-codegen</code> unit tests<br>\n  - 22 doctests<br>\n  - <code>cargo clippy -p cranelift-codegen --all-targets -- -D warnings</code><br>\n  - original WAST reproducer from #14053</p>\n</blockquote>",
